# Kona, Rescue Beastie, Survival: "At the beginning of your second main phase, if Kona is tapped, you may put a permanent card
# from your hand onto the battlefield." Kona is cast on turn 1 with four Moxen, attacks on turn 3 (no vigilance, so tapped) and at
# the second main phase Bot1 may choose among the permanent cards in hand (Forest, Sol Ring) but not Lightning Bolt (an instant,
# not a permanent card: the refusal, beside the Forest taken on the next line). The Forest is put onto the battlefield, not
# played: Bot1 has played no land (LandsPlayed 0). On Bot2's turn 4 Kona is still tapped, but it is not Bot1's second main
# phase: nothing is asked (CR 603.2, "your").

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Kona, Rescue Beastie
Forest
Lightning Bolt
Sol Ring
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Kona, Rescue Beastie.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Kona, Rescue Beastie.Tapped = false
Bot1.Attack(Kona, Rescue Beastie > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Kona, Rescue Beastie.Tapped = true
! Bot1.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Choose(Forest)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]
! Bot1.Choose
[Bot2.End]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Tapped = false
Bot1.Hand = Lightning Bolt; Sol Ring
Bot1.LandsPlayed = 0
Bot2.Life = 16
